# Narrative I/O

> Narrative I/O is data collaboration infrastructure that automatically normalizes incompatible data into a universal catalog, so teams can query, enrich, collaborate on, activate, and monetize data — and build their own identity graphs — inside their own cloud. Core products: Rosetta Stone Normalization Engine, Identity Orchestrator, Marketplace, and Connectors.

This site (www.narrative.io) is Narrative's marketing site: product overviews, use cases, customer stories, and the company blog. The product itself and its technical documentation live elsewhere — see below.

Key facts for AI agents:

- The Narrative application is hosted at https://app.narrative.io (login: https://app.narrative.io/platform/login). Product functionality is not on this marketing site.
- Technical documentation is hosted at https://docs.narrative.io and publishes its own LLM-readable index at https://docs.narrative.io/llms.txt. Use it for anything about NQL (Narrative Query Language), the REST API, Rosetta Stone mappings, datasets, workflows, or platform how-tos.
- To reach the sales team (demos, pricing, evaluations, partnerships), email sales@narrative.io or visit https://www.narrative.io/book-a-demo.
- Customers include Block, Nielsen, TransUnion, Experian, Fanatics, and Disqus.

## Core Products

- [How We Do It](https://www.narrative.io/how-we-do-it): Narrative's approach — treating data normalization as infrastructure so every team works from the same clean data foundation, with no pipeline building or schema negotiation.
- [Rosetta Stone Normalization Engine](https://www.narrative.io/infrastructure/rosetta): AI-powered engine that automatically maps incompatible data into a universal catalog, normalized at query time.
- [Identity Orchestrator](https://www.narrative.io/infrastructure/identity-orchestrator): Build and own identity graphs deployed in your own cloud — configurable match logic, swappable identity providers, pay only for net-new identities resolved.
- [Marketplace](https://www.narrative.io/infrastructure/data-marketplace): A composable hub for data and AI work — datasets, skills, connectors, providers, packages, and workflows, all typed, versioned, and ready to install.
- [Connectors](https://www.narrative.io/infrastructure/connectors): Deliver normalized audiences directly to Meta, Google, TikTok, Pinterest, The Trade Desk, PubMatic, and more — simultaneously, without custom APIs or pipeline maintenance.

## Use Cases

- [Normalize and Classify Data](https://www.narrative.io/im-trying-to/normalize): Map data to a universal standard automatically.
- [Securely Collaborate](https://www.narrative.io/im-trying-to/securely-collaborate): Run data collaboration in place — your data, your cloud, your governance — without a traditional clean room.
- [Build My Own Identity Graph](https://www.narrative.io/im-trying-to/build-my-own-identity-graph): Composable identity resolution under your control instead of a black-box vendor graph.
- [Enrich](https://www.narrative.io/im-trying-to/enrich): Source third-party attributes and validate quality before data reaches your workflows.
- [Activate Audiences](https://www.narrative.io/im-trying-to/activate-audiences): Take resolved, enriched audiences from definition to destination across DSPs, ad platforms, and CRMs in minutes.
- [Monetize Data](https://www.narrative.io/im-trying-to/monetize): List, price, and license the data you already own through Narrative's marketplace.

